The query in 1result.sql is safer because it uses ROW_NUMBER() to guarantee that exactly one “first‑payment” row is chosen per customer even when several payments share the same earliest timestamp, thereby preventing duplicate customer entries and skewed averages.  
The 0result.sql version relies only on the equality test with MIN(payment_date); if a customer has two (or more) payments at that same earliest time, the customer will be counted multiple times and the final aggregates will be incorrect.

```plaintext
1result.sql
